# Project Constitution and Master Engineering Prompt

The supreme governing document is `docs/PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md`. Read it first. Obey the constitutions. Preserve architecture. Identify root causes. Validate before completion. Never mark work complete without evidence.

Before any sprint, implementation, review, refactor, or bug fix, then read `docs/engineering/MASTER_ENGINEERING_PROMPT.md`. That file is the authoritative engineering standard. Follow it by default.

Then use `docs/engineering/README.md` (Engineering Index) for the Foundation Runbook, architecture, coding standards, branch strategy, release process, and sprint process.

- Never continue on an unhealthy foundation. Run the pre-flight checklist first.
- One logical change at a time. Reuse existing architecture. Never bypass validation.
- Find the root cause, explain why it occurred, and permanently prevent recurrence. Do not patch symptoms.
- Do not redesign Runtime, IDS, Capability Registry, Definition Registry, persistence, or Executive Environments unless that is the named programme.
- Never tell the founder a task is complete until it has been verified in the running application.
